  "prefLabel": "Res 5601.09 Permit Issuance Suspension",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Res 5601.09 Permit Issuance Suspension. The director shall, when he or she determines such suspension is necessary to reduce the imminent hazard, suspend the issuance of fire permits statewide or a portion thereof during periods of significant or prolonged forest fire activity and when the daily fire danger as determined by the division reaches a class 4 or 5.\n\nSource. #10547, eff 3-21-14",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/res5200-5900.html"
